 Act,\" addresses a broad range of programs and services administered by the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) and the Department of Defense. The legislation introduces changes to veteran compensation, education and economic opportunity, health care delivery, administrative organization, memorial affairs, and community care standards.","summary_threshold":50,"title":"Take Care of America’s Veterans Act","viability":58.9,"viability_status":"active"},"date":"2026-07-16","detail":"Related bill","id":"119-hr-9237","label":"H.R. 9237","title":"Take Care of America’s Veterans Act","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/9237"},{"card":{"analysis_status":"analyzed","bipartisan_band":"single","chamber":"Senate","cosponsor_count":7,"id":"119-s-4744","importance":85,"importance_band":"sweeping","introduced_date":"2026-06-10","is_demo":false,"label":"S. 4744","latest_action":{"date":"2026-06-11","text":"Read the second time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 433."},"policy_area":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsor":{"chamber":"Senate","district":null,"id":"M000934","name":"Sen. Moran, Jerry","party":"R","state":"KS"},"stage":"on_calendar","stage_label":"On a chamber calendar","summary":"S. 4744, the Take Care of America's Veterans Act, is a comprehensive federal bill addressing veterans' benefits, health care, counseling, Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) personnel, infrastructure, and community care programs. It introduces sweeping updates to disability compensation, education benefits, mental health and suicide prevention programs, community care access standards, and VA administrative and acquisition structures.","summary_threshold":50,"title":"Take Care of America’s Veterans Act","viability":40.7,"viability_status":"active"},"date":"2026-06-11","detail":"Related bill","id":"119-s-4744","label":"S. 4744","title":"Take Care of America’s Veterans Act","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/4744"}]},"selection":{"reason":"Impact scored and summarised by Gemini.","status":"analyzed"},"sources":{"latest":{"date":"2025-02-05","label":"Introduced in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1004/BILLS-119hr1004ih.htm"},"other":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1004"}],"past":[]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"9","id":"H001067","name":"Rep. Hudson, Richard","party":"R","state":"NC"},"stage":"reported","stage_label":"Reported by committee","summary":"The Love Lives On Act of 2025 extends and protects various benefit programs and services for surviving spouses of deceased members of the Armed Forces and veterans. Specifically, it ensures that remarrying does not disqualify a surviving spouse from receiving dependency and indemnity compensation, special pension benefits, or Survivor Benefit Plan annuities. Additionally, it expands the TRICARE definition of a dependent to include remarried widows or widowers whose subsequent marriages have ended.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"They can remarry without losing eligibility for certain benefits, compensation, pensions, and annuities.","group":"Surviving spouses of deceased members of the Armed Forces and veterans"},{"effect":"They are included in the definition of a dependent under the TRICARE program.","group":"Remarried widows and widowers whose subsequent marriage ended due to death, divorce, or annulment"}],"key_provisions":["The remarriage of a surviving spouse does not bar the furnishing of dependency and indemnity compensation or special pension benefits.","The Department of Defense may not terminate Survivor Benefit Plan annuity payments to a surviving spouse solely because of remarriage.","For certain surviving spouses who remarried before age 55 and before enactment, annuity payments are resumed one year after enactment or on the first day of the first month after enactment under specific conditions.","The TRICARE definition of a dependent is expanded to include a remarried widow or widower whose subsequent marriage ended due to death, divorce, or annulment."],"missing_information":["The exact financial cost of extending these benefits.","The precise number of individuals who will be newly eligible or have payments resumed.","Detailed administrative rules for how agencies will process resumed payments."],"plain_summary":"The Love Lives On Act of 2025 extends and protects various benefit programs and services for surviving spouses of deceased members of the Armed Forces and veterans. Specifically, it ensures that remarrying does not disqualify a surviving spouse from receiving dependency and indemnity compensation, special pension benefits, or Survivor Benefit Plan annuities. Additionally, it expands the TRICARE definition of a dependent to include remarried widows or widowers whose subsequent marriages have ended.","significance":"This legislation alters how remarriage impacts the military and veteran benefits of surviving spouses, ensuring that individuals do not lose compensation, pensions, annuities, or health care coverage solely because they remarry."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T07:24:06+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1004/BILLS-119hr1004ih.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Love Lives On Act of 2025","viability":64.4,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Reported by committee"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":21.0,"value":0.6,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"ava